silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_01_functors_as_typed_cross_kg_mappings_sections_04_typed_arrows_not_graph_edges_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'TypedArrowsNotGraphEdgesConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the pathological clinic node that absorbs all household nodes under a fixed-node graph hom; also, a derived anchor for the transport diagram: the clinic-side image of the household typed leg, carrying composition data.." .
